OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1788184560
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G2/2
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Tue 15 Sep to Tue 29 Sep
OL,6,FConfidence is very low from mid-
OL,7,FSeptember onwards. Initially, a
OL,8,Fcontinuation of the changeable pattern
OL,9,Fis most likely, with the wettest
OL,10,Fconditions in the northwest and longer
OL,11,Fdrier interludes in the southeast. As
OL,12,Fwe head further into September, the
OL,13,Fdistribution of rainfall becomes
OL,14,Fincreasingly uncertain at this range.
OL,15,FSettled or dry spells are still likely
OL,16,Fbetween weather systems. Temperatures
OL,17,Fare likely to be around average
OL,18,Foverall, although some warm spells are
OL,19,Fpossible, particularly in the south.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
